00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:23.663
Psych.

00:11:23.663 --> 00:11:25.140
Meanwhile, back in the United States,

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:29.000
they gotta keep up this white
savior liberation narrative

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:32.080
that they created to justify
going to war with Spain.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:35.890
So you see a lot more
theatrical PR by the government.

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:39.400
They staged this giant military
parade in New York City,

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:42.320
where this military Commander
who did the fake war,

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:44.160
George Dewey, marches down.

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:45.150
They called it Dewey Day.

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:47.320
It was like a two day
parade in New York City.

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:50.390
They created a big military arch for him.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:53.510
He became a military
hero for having liberated

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:55.710
all these people from the Spanish.

00:11:55.710 --> 00:11:58.720
And then you start to see
these crazy advertisements,

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:00.040
like the soap advertisement

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:03.190
that has George Dewey, the
Commander, washing his hands,

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:05.780
with the caption, quote,
the first step towards

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:07.870
lightening the white man's burden

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:11.113
is through teaching the
virtues of cleanliness.

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:15.470
And on the side, you have
soap being off-loaded

00:12:15.470 --> 00:12:18.490
in the Philippines and
being given to the locals.

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:21.500
The US had to frame this not as conquest,

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:23.960
but as the honorable duty of the US

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:25.830
to civilize these people,

00:12:25.830 --> 00:12:27.860
or in the words of the soap ad,

00:12:27.860 --> 00:12:31.003
quote, to brighten the
dark corners of the earth.

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:36.780
Geez, this is insane, and
was not that long ago.

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:39.410
Okay, so this is where
things really heat up.

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:43.460
It's 1900 now, Spain
loses the war, obviously.

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:47.350
And the US now owns Puerto Rico, Guam,

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:49.190
and they claim the Philippines.

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:51.570
But the local Filipinos,
who have been fighting

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:53.310
for their freedom for years are like,

00:12:53.310 --> 00:12:57.490
no, no, no, no, you just waltzed
in here, on our rebellion,

00:12:57.490 --> 00:12:58.880
and conspired with the Spanish

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:01.110
to make it look like
you were liberating us.

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:04.440
No, this is our country, we
don't need another colonizer.

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:06.182
And this is where things really heat up.

00:13:06.182 --> 00:13:08.765
(upbeat music)

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:18.747
The Filipinos start fighting
again for their independence.

00:13:18.747 --> 00:13:20.910
And this time, against the United States.

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:23.440
It is a pretty horrible bloody war,

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.070
one that I've never
learned about in school.

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:28.720
It include massacres of
men, women, and children

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:31.220
by the United States,
and hundred of thousands

00:13:31.220 --> 00:13:32.930
of civilian deaths.

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:36.730
But the US eventually won and
they established a government

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:37.740
in the Philippines.

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:40.340
Back in the US, the appetite for expansion

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:42.580
continued to go down,
and people sort of just

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:44.440
forgot about the Philippines.

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:45.980
They forgot that there was a war there.

00:13:45.980 --> 00:13:48.090
One newspaper summed it up by saying,

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:49.850
Americans didn't know if the Philippines

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:51.910
were islands or canned fruit.

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:54.720
But the fact remained
that the US went to war

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:56.980
and now owned the Philippines,

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:58.720
in addition to Puerto Rico and Guam.

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:00.730
So this begged a very important question,

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:03.140
one that hadn't been
asked before, which is,

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:05.630
is all of this land America?

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:07.820
Are these people Americans?

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.590
This was a huge question.

00:14:09.590 --> 00:14:11.550
And the answer to that questions

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:15.110
affects how we see these
territories still today.

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:17.380
Okay, so a few years after these wars,

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:20.730
there's a guy in New York
City who's importing oranges

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:22.780
from one of these
territories, Puerto Rico.

00:14:22.780 --> 00:14:24.590
And he's paying tariffs on these imports

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:28.050
because that's what you do
when you're importing oranges

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:29.180
from another country.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:31.830
Wait a minute, another country?

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:34.920
This guy was like, didn't
we conquer Puerto Rico,

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:36.520
and Guam, and the Philippines?

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:37.810
Isn't that America?

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:39.950
The Constitution says
that you can't put tariffs

00:14:39.950 --> 00:14:42.490
on stuff coming from
other parts of the US.

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:43.970
Like New Jersey can't put tariffs

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:46.360
on avocados from California.

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:49.720
So he sued and his case, and
a bunch of others like it,

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:51.060
made it to the Supreme Court.

00:14:51.060 --> 00:14:53.610
So now the Supreme Court must decide.

00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:56.430
Is this land, where we just won a war,

00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:57.400
is this America?

00:14:57.400 --> 00:14:58.620
Are these Americans?

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:00.580
If they are, do they
get all the same rights

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:02.130
as other Americans?

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:03.110
Do they get to vote?

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:04.950
Do they get to participate
in the US economy

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:05.980
without tariffs?

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:07.360
Like any other state does?

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:09.130
And honestly, this isn't a question

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:11.170
about oranges and tariffs.

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:13.450
The real question at stake here is,

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:16.190
is America the land of the free,

00:15:16.190 --> 00:15:18.100
where all are created equal?

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:20.100
Or are we an empire?

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:21.670
No different than any other empire

00:15:21.670 --> 00:15:24.710
that scoops up colonial
possessions in war,

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:27.700
and rules the people, who
are usually black and brown,

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:31.432
as subjects, not fully
a part of the country.

00:15:31.432 --> 00:15:33.210
That was the question that was at stake.

00:15:33.210 --> 00:15:36.160
And in these series of
cases in the early 1900,

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:39.150
the Supreme Court decided that America

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:42.150
was the latter, is the latter.

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:44.714
They created a new category of land called

00:15:44.714 --> 00:15:47.750
unincorporated territories,
where the people

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:50.160
don't have any representation
in the democracy,

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:53.150
but where Congress can
create laws on their own,

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:55.940
particularly laws dealing with revenue,

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:58.090
which would not be allowed
by the Constitution

00:15:58.090 --> 00:16:00.370
for states within the Union.

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:02.590
We can create revenue
laws, except that's totally

00:16:02.590 --> 00:16:04.740
unconstitutional for other
parts of our country.

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:06.810
In other words, unincorporated territories

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:10.080
are land we control and
exploit for revenue,

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:12.210
but whose people don't get to vote

00:16:12.210 --> 00:16:15.610
and don't get the right to trial by jury.

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:17.780
So, yeah, the Philippines,
in addition to Puerto Rico

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:21.100
and Guam, remained
unincorporated territories,

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:23.130
a place that the US could just ignore

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:24.670
without a lot of consequence.

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:26.900
They weren't important
enough or strategic enough

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:30.800
to be considered to become
states, like Hawaii or Alaska.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:34.640
So they sort of faded from
American consciousness.

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:36.800
Like, this is why we never
heard about this in school,

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:39.770
it didn't make it into the
history books in any salient way.

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:42.530
And how far the Philippines
had faded from people minds

00:16:42.530 --> 00:16:46.530
became very clear in December
of 1941, during World War II.

00:16:46.530 --> 00:16:49.790
The US had owned the
Philippines for like 40 years

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:53.150
when a fleet of Japanese
bombers flew across the Pacific

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:55.850
and bombed an American
naval base in Hawaii.

00:16:55.850 --> 00:16:58.621
- [Narrator] And the severe
bombing of Pearl Harbor

00:16:58.621 --> 00:17:02.970
by the enemy's planes
(indistinct) Japanese.

00:17:02.970 --> 00:17:04.800
But what we don't really
remember is on that day,

00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:08.050
Japan bombed Guam and the Philippines,

00:17:08.050 --> 00:17:11.130
two American territories,
as well as several other

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:13.250
American and British territories.

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:16.737
- Yesterday, December 7th,

00:17:18.353 --> 00:17:19.873
1941,

00:17:21.780 --> 00:17:25.870
a date which will live in infamy.

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:28.530
- Here is the draft of this speech.

00:17:28.530 --> 00:17:30.520
This is the original draft that FDR

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:33.060
spent the day marking
up before he gave it.

00:17:33.060 --> 00:17:35.740
Zoom-in a little bit and
you'll see on this draft

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:38.640
that it mentioned the
Philippines originally.

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:40.210
But FDR crossed it out.

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:43.140
He crossed out the mention of Manila.

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:45.900
Yes, the Philippines was
on some map somewhere.

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:48.630
Yes, we technically owned it.

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:50.480
But the people really
didn't want to hear about it

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:53.000
because these people weren't Americans.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:54.980
The Supreme Court had decided that.

00:17:54.980 --> 00:17:57.400
They weren't gonna become
states anytime soon,

00:17:57.400 --> 00:17:58.530
so why mention them?

00:17:58.530 --> 00:18:01.190
After that day, Japan actually full-on

00:18:01.190 --> 00:18:02.670
invaded the Philippines.

00:18:02.670 --> 00:18:03.730
They didn't do that to Hawaii.

00:18:03.730 --> 00:18:06.700
But they did to the Philippines,
until the end of the war.

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:08.380
At which point, the Philippines

00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:11.850
were finally granted independence in 1946.

00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:14.580
Fast forward to today, and this

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:17.840
we own you, but you're not
really Americans precedent,

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:19.490
established by the Supreme Court,

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:22.130
still applies to four million people

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:24.680
who live in unincorporated territories.

00:18:24.680 --> 00:18:26.090
Or let's just call a spade a spade,

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:27.230
let's call them what they are.

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:28.860
These are colonial possessions.

00:18:28.860 --> 00:18:30.880
The people who lived here don't experience

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:33.920
the full rule of law, they
don't get trial by jury,

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:37.260
they don't have full
representation in our democracy,

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:39.150
and they don't get to
vote for the President.

00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:42.120
This is why when a
hurricane hits Puerto Rico,

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:45.300
the government response is
not nearly what it should be.

00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:47.780
The way Trump talked about Puerto Rico

00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:50.870
as almost another country,
as not a part of us,

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:53.100
mirrors exactly how the Supreme Court

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:55.350
talked about this
unincorporated territories.

00:18:55.350 --> 00:18:58.410
They're for revenue, not to
compete with American farmers.

00:18:58.410 --> 00:19:01.710
We conquered these places,
but we didn't wanna bring

00:19:01.710 --> 00:19:04.800
the people fully into
the American project.

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:06.460
We left them out.

00:19:06.460 --> 00:19:08.409
And there, they remain today.

00:19:08.409 --> 00:19:10.909
(soft music)

